The verification code was extracted from Cattus, an app developed by OneOrThree, and
generalized for reuse. Account, server, reward and session code was removed.

This package bundles two TensorFlow Lite models from Google MediaPipe, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (assets/MODELS.md lists the source files and their SHA-256
hashes):

  - palm_detection_lite.tflite
    Google MediaPipe Palm Detection Lite
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-assets/palm_detection_lite.tflite
  - efficientdet_lite0_int8.tflite
    Google MediaPipe EfficientDet-Lite0 int8 v1
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/object_detector/efficientdet_lite0/int8/1/efficientdet_lite0.tflite

Source project: https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe

Expo templates
--------------

These files come from two Expo templates, expo-module-template (used by create-expo-module)
and expo-template-blank-typescript (the example app). Some are unchanged and some were
changed:

  - .gitignore, .prettierrc, eslint.config.cjs, tsconfig.json
  - example/.gitignore, example/babel.config.js, example/index.ts, example/metro.config.js,
    example/tsconfig.json
  - example/assets/ (the six default Expo icons and splash images)

